  "scene": {
    "id": "check-pilot4",
    "language": "[0]All right, so today, I'm going to be showing you checking. Uh, our goal is to get the ball into the goal, and right now, the opponent is[1] right in front of me. If he passed me the ball, I would not be able to directly get the ball into the goal, so this is bad. We need to do checking, which is letting me move somewhere else on the field, so then I can be in a more better position. So I'll go ahead and do that right now. I'm gonna move diagonally, and opponent's gonna follow me. [2][3]Then, you'll be passing me the ball. Oh. (laughs)[4] [5][6]Okay, then, you will have then passed the ball to me after I moved into a better position, and depending on my distance relative to the opponent, I can then either choose to pass the ball back to you or turn around the opponent and dribble it straight to the goal. In this case, I think that since I have a direct path to the goal, I could then dribble it straight to the goal without having to pass it back to you because you're still back over there. [7]And as you saw, that is why checking can be advantageous, because we just moved the position, and you're able to pass the ball to me, and I was pass, able to pass it back to the goal.",
